# Rust does not use glibc's _FORTIFY_SOURCE wrappers, so a Rust binary never
# carries the fortified symbols lintian looks for. The protection those
# wrappers provide against the class of bug they target is provided by the
# language instead. There is nothing to fix here and no flag that would change
# it.
fxsound-linux: hardening-no-fortify-functions [usr/bin/fxsound]
